CRITERION 4 — the four comments' factual claims hold against the code.
PASS on every command-verifiable claim; one sub-claim is design rationale and
is reported as unverifiable rather than passed on inspection.

  4a storage.go (atomicWrite, lines 570-582).
     "The rename below replaces whatever currently sits at path, symlink or
     not ... the file the link used to point at is left untouched and silently
     stops receiving further writes" — proven by Criterion 2's test.
     "cannot stay atomic if the target lives on a different filesystem than
     the link" — demonstrated: /tmp is ext4 and /dev/shm is tmpfs per
     `df -T /tmp /dev/shm`; `go run /tmp/t6check/exdev.go` ->
       os.Rename(/tmp/... -> /dev/shm/...) err = invalid cross-device link
     "resolving the symlink first would relocate staging to the target's
     directory ... would add a resolve-to-rename race to the most
     safety-critical write path in the package" — this is counterfactual
     design rationale about code that does not exist. NO COMMAND CAN
     DEMONSTRATE IT; I did not pass it on inspection. It is consistent with
     the actual body (os.CreateTemp(dir, ...) where dir = filepath.Dir(path),
     storage.go:594) but that is reasoning, not evidence.

  4b config.go (SaveUserSettings, lines 168-176).
