OBSERVATION (non-blocking, for the lead's judgement, not a criterion failure).
The README's final clause is an imperative — "Don't point symlinks into or out
of `data/`." The "out of" direction is exactly what Criteria 2 and 3 prove. The
"into" direction (an external symlink whose TARGET is a path inside data/) I
probed directly:
/tmp/t6check/repo/internal/services/storage/zz_t6_into_check_test.go,
TestT6_Probe_SymlinkPointingIntoDataDir ->
  PROBE RESULT: external symlink still a symlink=true; reading through it
  yields "V2" (dest was replaced by rename at the same path)
i.e. an inbound symlink keeps working across a Storage save, because the rename
republishes at the same path. This does not falsify anything the README
asserts: the assertive sentence is the preceding one, and "Don't ..." is
prescriptive advice that can be conservative without being untrue. Recording it
as a fact so the lead adjudicates rather than discovers it later.

Under the claim shape stated in the brief — the README asserts only that
symlinks in data/ are unsupported and that BOTH failure modes exist, with no
completeness claim — every assertion made is backed by command output above.
